msgstr ""

#: ../../../SourceLevelDebugging.md:1534
msgid ""
"Also, it is common practice in ObjC to have different property declarations "
"in the `@interface` and `@implementation` - e.g. to provide a read-only "
"property in the interface, and a read-write interface in the "
"implementation.  In that case, the compiler should emit whichever property "
"declaration will be in force in the current translation unit."
